## ASSEMBLED SECTION



### <img src="https://flagcdn.com/fr.svg" width="32" alt="France" style={{display: 'inline', verticalAlign: 'middle', position: 'relative', top: '-2px', marginRight: '8px', border: '1px solid #d1d5db', borderRadius: '2px'}} />France

France continues navigating structural governance instability while maintaining international positioning as leader of European resistance to American pressure. Domestically, the government depends entirely on Article 49.3 to pass basic legislation, with PM Lecornu using the mechanism for the third time on the 2026 budget while carefully managing 2027 electoral calendar pressures. The July 7, 2026 Le Pen appeal verdict remains the critical binary event determining 2027 election dynamics, with tactical maneuvering accelerating across the political spectrum. Internationally, France sustains its confrontational stance toward US coercion through sharp diplomatic disagreements with NATO leadership, strategic territorial solidarity (Greenland consulate), and innovative communication strategies, while continuing multilateral responsibilities through G7 presidency. The central tension persists between France's European leadership ambitions and domestic political fragmentation that undermines institutional credibility.

**Key developments:**

- **Domestic:** PM engaged government responsibility three times to pass 2026 budget without parliamentary votes, surviving six motions of censure from opposition parties. Budget adopted despite strong resistance, demonstrating complete dependence on constitutional workarounds.
- **Domestic:** Le Pen acknowledged possible unintentional errors while maintaining innocence in EU parliamentary assistants case. Changed strategy from first trial, but evidence remains damaging with July 7 verdict determining 2027 candidacy eligibility.
- **Domestic:** Mélenchon used far-right terminology 'grand remplacement' in Toulouse speech, claiming to represent France's demographic renewal. Provoked reactions from Bardella and Zemmour, demonstrating tactical provocation to highlight far-right ideological positions.
- **Diplomatic:** Foreign Ministry activated 'French Response' X account as information warfare tool using irony and memes to counter international attacks, targeting US, Russian, and other foreign actors. Account gained 145,000 followers and represents unprecedented diplomatic communication strategy.
- **Diplomatic:** France appointed Jean-Noël Poirier to establish consulate in Nuuk opening February 6, in direct response to Trump's Greenland territorial ambitions. Represents territorial solidarity with Denmark and assertion of European autonomy against US coercion.

<Accordion title="Other Stories">
- **Macron's sunglasses moment at Davos goes viral with 'for sure' meme** — Emmanuel Macron's appearance at Davos wearing blue aviator sunglasses due to an eye condition, combined with his repeated use of 'for sure' in English, became a global internet meme. He later stopped wearing the sunglasses publicly. *([rtl.fr](https://rtl.fr/actu/politique/apres-son-probleme-a-l-oeil-emmanuel-macron-apparait-sans-lunettes-de-soleil-pour-la-premiere-fois-depuis-le-15-janvier-7900595372))*
- **Lecornu plans government reshuffle after budget adoption** — PM Sébastien Lecornu announced plans for an 'adjustment' of his government team following budget adoption, partly due to ministers departing for municipal campaigns including Culture Minister Rachida Dati. *([lemonde.fr](https://lemonde.fr/politique/article/2026/01/29/sebastien-lecornu-veut-profiter-des-elections-municipales-pour-remanier-son-gouvernement_6664597_823448.html))*
- **Marine Le Pen appeal trial continues with changed defense strategy** — Marine Le Pen's appeal trial for the European parliamentary assistants case proceeded through January with the defendant adopting a softer defense strategy, acknowledging possible unintentional errors while maintaining innocence. *([lemonde.fr](https://lemonde.fr/politique/article/2026/02/01/marine-le-pen-prevenue-la-semaine-cheffe-de-parti-le-week-end-la-double-vie-de-la-leader-du-rn_6664944_823448.html))*
- **RN boycotts Morandini show after host's conviction** — Jordan Bardella ordered RN officials to stop appearing on Jean-Marc Morandini's CNews show following the host's definitive conviction for corruption of minors, reversing the party's initial continued participation. *([franceinfo.fr](https://franceinfo.fr/politique/front-national/les-elus-rn-pries-de-ne-plus-participer-a-l-emission-de-jean-marc-morandini-sur-cnews-apres-sa-condamnation-definitive-pour-corruption-de-mineurs_7766117.html))*
- **Jordan Bardella rumored relationship with Italian princess sparks media attention** — Rumors circulated about RN president Jordan Bardella's relationship with Princess Maria Carolina de Bourbon des Deux-Siciles after they were spotted together at Paris events, though Bardella declined to comment on his private life. *([gala.fr](https://rtl.fr/actu/politique/ma-vie-privee-m-appartient-sur-rtl-jordan-bardella-esquive-avec-le-sourire-une-question-sur-maria-carolina-de-bourbon-des-deux-siciles-7900595236))*
- **NATO chief sparks French anger over European defense capabilities** — NATO Secretary-General Mark Rutte told the European Parliament that Europe cannot defend itself without US help, prompting sharp rebuttals from French officials who insisted Europeans can and must take charge of their own security. *([sudouest.fr](https://radiofrance.fr/franceinter/podcasts/geopolitique/geopolitique-du-mercredi-28-janvier-2026-5065749))*
- **Mélenchon calls for Russia's return to Europe and Nord Stream restart** — Jean-Luc Mélenchon proposed bringing Russia back into the European concert and restarting the Nord Stream gas pipelines, arguing this would reduce energy prices and that Europe shouldn't be forced to buy American gas. *([leparisien.fr](https://leparisien.fr/politique/melenchon-veut-ramener-la-russie-dans-le-concert-europeen-et-remettre-les-gazoducs-nord-stream-en-route-28-01-2026-EIZWSGI7CBHFHG25V42O7IJ64A.php))*
- **Banking error causes thousands of duplicate transactions across French banks** — A technical error at Monext, a Crédit Mutuel Arkéa subsidiary, caused thousands of duplicate card payments to appear on accounts at multiple French banks including Caisse d'Épargne, Banque Populaire, and BoursoBank. *([francebleu.fr](https://francebleu.fr/infos/economie-social/incident-bancaire-de-nombreux-clients-preleves-par-erreur-que-faire-si-vous-etes-concerne-8991210))*
- **Bardella and Marion Maréchal signal political reconciliation** — Jordan Bardella and Marion Maréchal appeared together at the launch of her book 'Si tu te sens Le Pen', signaling a strategic rapprochement between the RN president and the influential far-right figure ahead of 2027 elections. *([lepoint.fr](https://lepoint.fr/politique/marion-marechal-et-jordan-bardella-se-rapprochent-a-un-an-de-la-presidentielle-2027-C7RQI7D5B5DYHJSFQQ35DGHBM4))*
- **Defense Ministry theft investigation involves cybersecurity official** — Three men including a Defense Ministry cybersecurity official were arrested for theft and possession of stolen multimedia equipment during a transfer operation in Courbevoie. *([lefigaro.fr](https://lefigaro.fr/faits-divers/trois-hommes-dont-un-agent-du-ministere-des-armees-interpelles-pour-vol-et-recel-de-materiel-multimedias-20260129))*
- **Municipal elections campaign intensifies with Mélenchon targeting small business owners** — Jean-Luc Mélenchon launched outreach efforts to small business owners while intensifying LFI's municipal campaigns, including a major rally in Roubaix and plans for meetings in other cities like Montpellier. *([lemonde.fr](https://lemonde.fr/politique/article/2026/01/30/jean-luc-melenchon-tente-de-seduire-les-petits-patrons_6664714_823448.html))*
</Accordion>---

